sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch09-19> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The ultimate rules for the universe will produce networks that look largely random at small scales, and this randomness is what allows a definite and robust dimensionality of 3 to emerge for space.";
    dc:type "physical-hypothesis";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Small-scale randomness in the network makes space robustly 3D";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 9, “Fundamental Physics”; section “Evolution of Networks” (from p. 508), p. 515. Scope: network models of space and the dimensionality of physical space"
}
